From 81fcd6e5c61eb50847ebca9803a2120b410e3075 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mehedi <growwithmh@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:17:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix authenticated boot, view persistence and rejoin flow
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three production bugs with one shape: the app was making decisions before it
knew enough.

Stale data flash
- localLoad() painted the previous, pre-auth local cache and the built-in
  inventory defaults, then the Supabase snapshots replaced them. In live mode
  the local cache is no longer read at all: Supabase is authoritative for
  tasks, team, meetings, inventory, meta and reports, and localStorage keeps
  only preferences.
- A branded loading shell covers the app while the session, profile, site and
  every collection resolve. PB.warmup() fills the caches before the first
  paint, so the first render is the real project.

View persistence
- setView("board") ran at boot and again after auth, so the restored view
  either never applied or applied after Board had already painted. The view is
  now chosen once, after resolution and before the first render, and only a
  real navigation is remembered — nothing during boot may write.
- Key is build-board:view:<site>:<member>; an unknown value falls back to Board.

Rejoin
- loadProfile() treated zero memberships as a failure, so a removed member
  holding a valid invitation was told to ask an admin before the invitation was
  ever tried. Zero memberships is now a modelled state, a pending invitation is
  always consumed first, and the token survives sign-in via sessionStorage.
- accept_invite() reports which thing went wrong — unknown, wrong address,
  expired, already used — and accepting twice is a no-op rather than an error.
  The account, people row and permanent board key are untouched; only a
  membership returns, and ensureOwnTeamProfile() reactivates the roster row.
- A genuinely project-less account gets a proper screen with a way out.

One idempotent CREATE OR REPLACE is required in production; no table, column
or policy changes. See supabase/migrations/2026-09-13-accept-invite-rejoin.sql.

115 tests passing.

